--- begin ---
PRE-REGISTRATION: traced NOP copy of the YOLOv8s control, shim view. Desktop 2 (DESKTOP-CBL5NUA), 2026-10-15.
Written before any traced dispatch of the NOP copy. build/yolov8s_tr_ctl_nop.ignite = tools/engine_dispatch_floor
.write_nop_copy of build/yolov8s_tr_ctl.ignite (3,114 weight packets, header op set to NOP; instruction stream, xclbin
and trace manifest unchanged). It has not been dispatched.

Question (from the shim budget, results/aie/shim_trace_budget_yolov8s_desktop2_20261015T1922Z): on the compute-heavy
layers the MemTile pushes back on the activation stream 20% of the window. Is that the arithmetic? Do weights stay
ahead with no arithmetic? Is the unexplained residual compute-related?

Method. scratch/b45/sit_nop.py --rounds 6: per round ctl and nop (order alternated), each a separate process running
tools/engine_shim_trace.py --runs 1 (cold first dispatch, logical column 0). Under research-lowlevel.sh --npu; void
unless timing_eligible true. Then tools/shim_trace_budget.py on each arm (same build dir: the NOP copy's insts.bin is
the control's), then scratch/b45/verdict.py. Groups are FIXED from the committed control budget's warm compute share
(13 Oct real/NOP): lo < 10% (18 layers), mid 10-35% (17), hi >= 35% (31). Fractions are window-weighted per group.

Gates (if either fails, P1-P3 are not read):
- C, calibration: NOP/ctl frame windows 0.70-0.82 (warm 13 Oct: 12.29/16.14 = 0.76), and the lo group's windows
  NOP/ctl 0.90-1.10 (those layers have <10% compute).
- S, stability: this sitting's ctl hi-group activation backpressure 15-25% (the earlier sitting read 20%).

Predictions and rules:
- P1 (is the MemTile fill compute?): NOP hi-group A_bp <= 5% -> COMPUTE; >= 15% -> NOT COMPUTE (a stage below the
  MemTile other than the arithmetic: the MemTile-to-core split, core DMA or lock handshake); else PARTIAL.
  Expected: COMPUTE.
- P2 (are weights ahead without compute?): NOP W_bp over the 62 layers whose control weights move > 5% of the window:
  >= 45% -> AHEAD WITHOUT COMPUTE (weight backpressure is set by activation delivery/handshake, not arithmetic);
  < 30% -> WAITED ON COMPUTE; else BETWEEN. Expected: AHEAD WITHOUT COMPUTE (the 18 lo layers already read 60%).
- P3 (the activation residual, A_resid ~ a_tasks + const per arm):
  P3a per-task coefficient NOP/ctl within +-25% -> UNCHANGED (the per-task part is not compute: issue gaps or a slow
  strided rate); < 0.5 -> SHRANK; else CHANGED.
  P3b per-layer constant NOP/ctl < 0.5 -> SHRANK (the tail was compute); within +-25% -> UNCHANGED; else CHANGED.
  Expected: P3a UNCHANGED, P3b SHRANK. No expectation is strong; the residual is DERIVED (rate and clock).
Named alternatives: the NOP copy changes only the arithmetic (and the cores' cycle count per packet); data volume,
tasks, issue order and trace setup are identical. A changed DDR/thermal state between arms is controlled by
interleaving. Reported, not verdict-bearing: every other fraction, per layer.

A hang, a refused trace or contention voids the sitting; no rerun of the same design without a new pre-registration.
